version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-21"
keywords:
  - durian
  - plant disease classification
  - out-of-distribution detection
  - open-set rejection
  - JPEG compression
  - shortcut learning
  - smartphone application
abstract: >-
  Code and pre-specified experiments for a study of out-of-scope rejection in
  smartphone durian disease classifiers. A classifier with about 96% accuracy and
  an AUROC of about 0.99 labelled about 43% of reduced, JPEG-compressed
  out-of-scope images as diseased under the top-1 rule. Pre-specified experiments
  traced the failure to JPEG compression rather than resolution.
